      "rationale": "Both operands range over two, three and four digits, including a case where the subtrahend is as small as 90, and the estimate is asked for through several response modes rather than only one."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "rationale": "Across every choice item the distractors are the key offset by one or two, as with the four options clustered around 400 and those clustered around 2000. Since only a round number can be an estimate, the correct option is identifiable without performing any rounding or subtraction at all, which empties the item of its intended cognitive content."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Four distinct presentations occur: the estimate-the-difference question, the approximation cloze written with the wavy equals sign, a truth judgement about 7902 minus 480, and the error-checking items attributed to Grace, Rico and Liza."
    },
    "competency_alignment": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Some generated pairs make the estimate actively misleading. At seed 600 the true difference between 5646 and 5190 is a few hundred, yet the accepted estimate is 1000, more than double it. Rewarding an estimate that misrepresents the answer by that margin teaches the wrong habit, and the set offers no item where closeness of the operands is treated as a reason to estimate differently."
    },
    "scale_appropriateness": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Operands honour the up to four digits wording, the largest being 9413, and the estimated differences stay within the range this quarter's subtraction work already covers."
